.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-COLLECT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-collect
.Nd record what the kernel, ZFS, eBPF, Kubernetes and the host report, once a minute, as JSON lines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs a fixed set of read-only commands and appends each one's output,
with the time, host, cluster, exit status and duration, as one JSON line
to a file of its own:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/var/lib/kldload/training-corpus/YYYY-MM-DD/<command, as a file name>.jsonl
.Ed
.Pp
The commands cover the loaded eBPF programs, maps and attachments;
Cilium's status, load-balancer and connection-tracking tables, map
pressure, endpoints and identities, and Tetragon's tracing policies and
five seconds of its events, where they run; the pools, the ARC,
snapshots and the ZFS debug log; Kubernetes nodes, pods, services,
policies, usage and events when a cluster answers; and the host's load,
memory, disk, established connections, kernel messages, virtual machines
and GPU.
Each runs for at most five seconds.
Output that is JSON is also stored parsed, as
.Li output_struct .
.Pp
.Pa kldload-collect.timer
runs it a minute after boot and every minute after that.
Day directories older than
.Ev KLDLOAD_COLLECT_KEEP_DAYS
are removed at the end of each run.
.Pp
It was written to collect a record of the machine's own behaviour to
train the web console's assistant on; nothing in kldload reads the
corpus today.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Set in the environment or in
.Pa /etc/kldload/collect.conf .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_COLLECT_DIR
The corpus directory; default
.Pa /var/lib/kldload/training-corpus .
.It Ev KLDLOAD_COLLECT_TIMEOUT
Seconds each command may take; default 5.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_COLLECT_HOST , Ev KLDLOAD_COLLECT_CLUSTER
The host and cluster written into each record; default the host name, and
.Pa /etc/kldload/cluster
or the host name.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_COLLECT_KEEP_DAYS
Days of corpus kept; default 30, and 0 keeps everything.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kldload/collect.conf
Settings, read as shell by root.
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/training-corpus/
The corpus.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0; a command that fails is recorded with its exit status, and the run
goes on.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30.
.Ss One day's files, and one record
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# ls /var/lib/kldload/training-corpus/2026-09-30
bpftool-j-map-show.jsonl
bpftool-j-net-show.jsonl
bpftool-j-prog-show.jsonl
cat-proc-loadavg.jsonl
\&...
virsh-list-all.jsonl
zfs-list-t-snapshot-o-name-used-creation-s-creation.jsonl
zpool-list-o-name-size-alloc-free-frag-cap-dedup-health.jsonl
# tail -1 /var/lib/kldload/training-corpus/2026-09-30/cat-proc-loadavg.jsonl | python3 -m json.tool
{
    "ts": "2026-09-30T07:18:21Z",
    "host": "onyx",
    "cluster": "onyx",
    "cmd": "cat /proc/loadavg",
    "desc": "Load avg (raw kernel)",
    "category": "host",
    "exit_code": 0,
    "duration_ms": 8,
    "output_text": "26.37 23.41 14.18 25/2351 3616168"
}
.Ed
.Ss What it costs
Before retention existed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# du -sh /var/lib/kldload/training-corpus
874M	/var/lib/kldload/training-corpus
.Ed
.Pp
That was 32 days.
.Ss Keeping less, or none
Not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# echo 'KLDLOAD_COLLECT_KEEP_DAYS=7' >> /etc/kldload/collect.conf
# systemctl disable --now kldload-collect.timer
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr systemd.timer 5 ,
.Xr bpftool 8 ,
.Xr kldload-debug-bundle 8 ,
.Xr kldload-doctor 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: nothing removed the corpus, and a
desktop had 874 MB of it after a month.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
.Pa collect.conf
is run as shell, as root: only root should be able to write it.
.Pp
Connection lists and kernel messages are recorded as they are.
